cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the dissertation and the archived software release."
title: "ARSPI-Net: An Interpretable Neuromorphic Framework for Clinical EEG Analysis"
authors:
  - family-names: Lane
    given-names: Andrew A.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheAwesomeAndy/dissoAdventureExperiments"
url: "https://github.com/TheAwesomeAndy/dissoAdventureExperiments"
abstract: >-
  Software and experiments accompanying the PhD dissertation "Affective
  Reservoir-Spike Processing and Inference Network (ARSPI-Net): A Four-Level
  Interpretable Neuromorphic Framework for Clinical EEG Analysis." ARSPI-Net
  transforms multichannel EEG into an explicit hierarchy of temporal,
  dynamical, and graph-organized representations whose intermediate quantities
  remain inspectable. Headline classification results are corrected
  confirmatory estimates (five repeats of five-fold participant-grouped
  cross-validation, fold-local preprocessing, data-independent SRP-64
  projection). Passing unit tests verify code behavior, not scientific
  validity.
keywords:
  - neuromorphic computing
  - spiking neural networks
  - reservoir computing
  - EEG
  - interpretability
  - affective computing
